{
  "_note": "Each preset is a complete LoweringSpec dict plus two catalogue blocks: `match` (what makes a tree use the framework: import roots / base classes / decorators — catalog.detect) and `dispatch` (the framework's dispatch methods and the impl methods they forward to — engine_walls S3, the IPCMethods.txt analogue). Copy the LoweringSpec part into SPEC_JSON for a hand-written run, or let draft.py derive it. Presence of any general key opts into general mode; the autogpt_legacy preset uses the legacy keys. dispatch rows are matched by dotted suffix: keep enough of the module path to make them framework-specific (BaseTool.__call__ exists in several frameworks). `match.imports` entries are dotted PREFIXES of imported modules (plus the imported name for `from m import n`): use a discriminating one (`app.tool`, `agents.function_tool`), never a bare top-level name that any project may have as its own package (`app`, `agents`) — review M4.",
